    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0863" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1203: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-17T12:00:00+02:35">September 17,
                            1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. The message in your 56, September 12, 6 p.m., and the statement in circular
                    September 13th<anchor n="74" xml:id="d633-f1"/> have created a most excellent
                    impression and are gratefully appreciated.</p>
                <p>My informant states that the inquiry in my 92<anchor n="75" xml:id="d633-f2"/>
                    was based on the assumption that League action would fail and was not intended
                    to request American diplomatic intervention except as a last resort to avert
                    war. The Emperor seems prepared to go the utmost limit of concession compatible
                    with national honor and dignity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d633-f1" n="74" xml:id="d633-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it contained summary of the Secretary’s statement to the press, of
                    September 12, 1935, <ref target="#pg746">p. 746</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d633-f2" n="75" xml:id="d633-f2-content">
                <p>September 10, 3 p.m., <ref target="#pg744">p. 744</ref>.</p>
